  m_Name: SO_Rhino
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AnimalData
  id: rhino
  displayName: Black Rhino
  habitat: Thick scrub and bushland. See them at Ol Pejeta Conservancy.
  status: Critically Endangered (IUCN Red List)
  fact: Kenya's black rhino population has more than doubled, from fewer than 400
    in the 1980s to over 1,000, according to Kenya Wildlife Service figures reported
    by WWF. Years of conservation work drove the rise.
  viewingTip: Switch the camera flash off and keep quiet. Rhinos see poorly, so a
    sudden noise is all it takes for one to charge. Never step between a cow and
    her calf.
  warningLine: The rhino is snorting. Move away quietly.
  viewingRadius: 18
  dangerRadius: 8
  callClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1772f50f4efaa734f851d0002b8554c4, type: 3}
